---
Title: Prose that looks like code
---

Each paragraph below once stopped the build or garbled its own sentence. An
exported name claims only a call or a member; anything else stays prose.

Save the Date. Bring wine.

I saved the Date.

Math.PI + 1, and more.

Math.max(1, 2) + 3 is five.

The math.sqrt(x) function takes one argument.

function(x) is how this paragraph begins.

The func(x) notation is common.

Genuine calls still run: calc("2+2"), four, which is nice.

It is calc("2+2"), four.

Pi is Math.PI.
